`},{type:"paragraph",raw:"The source surface is only as wide as its longest line. The frame fits the content or available columns, and only the source scrolls horizontally. Copy returns the original text. The number gutter, tab and borders stay outside selection.",text:"The source surface is only as wide as its longest line. The frame fits the content or available columns, and only the source scrolls horizontally. Copy returns the original text. The number gutter, tab and borders stay outside selection.",tokens:[{type:"text",raw:"The source surface is only as wide as its longest line. The frame fits the content or available columns, and only the source scrolls horizontally. Copy returns the original text. The number gutter, tab and borders stay outside selection.",text:"The source surface is only as wide as its longest line. The frame fits the content or available columns, and only the source scrolls horizontally. Copy returns the original text. The number gutter, tab and borders stay outside selection.",escaped:!1}]},{type:"space",raw:`

`},{type:"paragraph",raw:"Syntax colors and resolved identifier links come from build-time TypeScript metadata. Comments, strings, keywords and unresolved names keep their syntax color. A visible blue underline appears only when that exact occurrence has a semantic anchor; CSS supplies aqua hover without mouse state.",text:"Syntax colors and resolved identifier links come from build-time TypeScript metadata. Comments, strings, keywords and unresolved names keep their syntax color. A visible blue underline appears only when that exact occurrence has a semantic anchor; CSS supplies aqua hover without mouse state.",tokens:[{type:"text",raw:"Syntax colors and resolved identifier links come from build-time TypeScript metadata. Comments, strings, keywords and unresolved names keep their syntax color. A visible blue underline appears only when that exact occurrence has a semantic anchor; CSS supplies aqua hover without mouse state.",text:"Syntax colors and resolved identifier links come from build-time TypeScript metadata. Comments, strings, keywords and unresolved names keep their syntax color. A visible blue underline appears only when that exact occurrence has a semantic anchor; CSS supplies aqua hover without mouse state.",escaped:!1}]},{type:"space",raw:`

